      </Table>
      <p>The sequence gives the previous and next links, the reltable gives the typed groups, the hand-written external link survives as "Related information", and <code>@linking="targetonly"</code> leaves the noise task with no links at all while the recording task still links to it.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p><code>project-health</code> checks the reltable like any other reference. Misspell <code>topics/exporting-audio.dita</code> in the second <code>&lt;relrow&gt;</code> as <code>topics/export-audio.dita</code> and run the gate:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"== project-health  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\nRoot map: audacity-guide.ditamap (project config); house rules: none (none configured)\nBroken references (1):\n  /home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:56  @href=\"topics/export-audio.dita\"\n\nSummary\n  Broken references             1\nFAIL: project-health found issues"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>After each error exercise, undo the deliberate change and rerun the gate. Confirm that it prints <code>STAGE OK</code> before continuing.</p>
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li>Nested <code>&lt;topicref&gt;</code>s make a hierarchy; <code>@collection-type="family"</code> and <code>"sequence"</code> say how children relate, and the output links accordingly.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;topicgroup&gt;</code> groups without a heading; <code>&lt;topichead&gt;</code> is a heading.</li>
      <li><code>@linking</code> controls which links a topic gives and receives; <code>@locktitle="yes"</code> with <code>&lt;navtitle&gt;</code> changes the table of contents but not the page.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;reltable&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;relheader&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;relcolspec type&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;relrow&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;relcell&gt;</code> state relationships once for both directions, typed by information type.</li>
      <li>Use <code>&lt;related-links&gt;</code> for relationships that belong with the topic.</li>
      </ul>
